          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "n "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Take a convex mirror. Hold it in one hand.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.125,
            0.141,
            0.618,
            0.156
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "n "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Hold a pencil in the upright position in the other hand.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.124,
            0.156,
            0.698,
            0.184
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Observe the image of the pencil in the mirror. Is the image erect or inverted? Is it diminished or enlarged?",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.125,
            0.184,
            0.698,
            0.214
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Move the pencil away from the mirror slowly. Does the image become smaller or larger?",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.124,
            0.213,
            0.698,
            0.259
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Repeat this Activity carefully. State whether the image will move closer to or farther away from the focus as the object is moved away from the mirror?",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.099,
            0.276,
            0.724,
            0.374
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "We consider two positions of the object for studying the image formed by a convex mirror. First is when the object is at infinity and the second position is when the object is at a finite distance from the mirror. The ray diagrams for the formation of image by a convex mirror for these two positions of the object are shown in Fig.9.8 (a) and (b), respectively. The results are summarised in Table 9.2.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.131,
            0.384,
            0.911,
            0.536
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 7,
              "bbox": [
                0.131,
                0.384,
